{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"705af8910d4adc695f4e78b285734a882caa899efea36ddb98e3ed928800c3fc"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":78333,"output_tokens":2300,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how an image-pull failure that occurs inside the buildah scan script is classified as ScannerUnavailableError (e.g. detect a non-zero exec exit code with no parseable JSON, or a pull-specific marker, and raise ScannerUnavailableError), so the Context's transient-image-pull claim actually holds; add a unit test covering a pull failure surfacing as a retryable failure rather than a finding.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Context: 'Left unclassified, a transient image pull would be recorded as a security finding and block promotion.'","Plan: 'A pod that cannot be created, pulled, or reached is infrastructure failing' and 'PodCommandRunner.__call__ therefore catches PodEngineError from create, wait_ready, copy_in, and exec_capture, and re-raises it as ScannerUnavailableError.'","scan_script runs `buildah from <image>` under `set -e` inside the pod; a pull failure exits the script non-zero. _exec_capture_sync returns (returncode, stdout, stderr) and never raises PodEngineError on a non-zero inner script exit — only kubectl-exec transport failure would. So a failed pull returns CommandResult(returncode!=0), which RealSemgrepScanner/RealTrivyScanner raise as ScannerError, which SecurityMediator.scan converts into a finding (fails closed) instead of ScannerUnavailableError (retry)."],"finding":"The plan's infrastructure-failure classification does not actually cover the transient image-pull case it names, because the pull runs inside the buildah script and surfaces as a non-zero CommandResult.returncode rather than a PodEngineError.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f546aa13bc2f9928f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'Classifying infrastructure failure'; scanner_pod.py scan_script + PodCommandRunner.__call__","norm_id":"nebdd29c6be15f9d0","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient registry/pull error while pulling the pinned semgrep or trivy image during a scan","buildah short-name or TLS failure pulling the image inside the pod"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how new pod failure points (pull/create/wait-ready/exec re-raised as ScannerUnavailableError) are logged or metered so operators can see and debug retried scans.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T5e","T6","T9","necessity"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'PodCommandRunner.__call__ therefore catches PodEngineError ... and re-raises it as ScannerUnavailableError'","No mention of logging/metric when a pod fails to create/pull/reach or when teardown runs on failure"],"finding":"The plan introduces new pod-based failure points (image pull, pod create, wait-ready, exec) but does not state how these failures are observed by operators — no metric/log/trace for ScannerUnavailableError re-raises or pod teardown.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f11b9eb8c0af7d36e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Classifying infrastructure failure","norm_id":"n7487ae92242418e8","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A transient image-pull failure repeatedly triggers activity retries with no operator-visible signal of why scans are slow/failing"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so ea